            "index": 0,
            "finish_reason": "stop",
            "message": {
              "role": "assistant",
              "content": "QA Lantern Witness lifts the bone whistle to her lips and blows. The sound is thin at first, then sharpens into a steady, rising tone that cuts through the wind like a blade. She holds it for three seconds, drops it to a lower note, and lets it fade.\n\n“Three high, one low, repeat,” she says. “In whiteout, the markers won’t show. The whistle carries farther than shouting and doesn’t freeze your lungs.”\n\nShe tucks the whistle back into her satchel without offering it. “You keep your eyes on the stones and your pace steady. That’s enough.”\n\nQA Cinder Witness watches, arms crossed, then mutters, “Show-off,” and turns her face back to the path."
            }
          }
        ]
      }
